{
 "spec": "rig-pose-map alternates — DRAFT for rig-c/pose#6 (HQ, 2026-10-13); not a released format — k0 copy with K0 added — polish1_arms copy: K2 left arm moved to forearm_l_mid / upperarm_l_mid (in front of the jacket, behind the right arm), hands split along the painted boundary",
 "rig": "polish1_arms/build/skeleton.json",
 "conventions": {
  "set": "an alternate is a set: every slot in `slots` switches to its attachment together, every slot in `hides` goes empty (null), and nothing of another set stays shown. Selection is driven by `chains` (the arms). `hides` lists every alternate-bearing slot this set does not use, so a direct switch from another set clears that set's slots without the map needing to know which set was showing",
  "drawn": "per bone: world_deg = the segment's direction in the set painting (Spine world, y up, counter-clockwise from +x), read from the painting's own RTMPose joints (`drawn_from`), NOT from the key skeleton (`pose`), which differs by up to 20.8 deg (K1 forearms; see report). rotate_key_deg = local_deg - setup_local_deg: the bone's rotate key that poses it at its drawn angle. While the set shows, the bone's key is rotate_key_deg + (reference - drawn) — pose#6's rule",
  "place": "each slot carries its own place in the setup draw order of the built rig (index of 35; `after`/`before` are its neighbours). The place is a property of the SLOT, not a key: switching sets is attachment keys only, no drawOrder timeline. A segment whose measured place differs from the base piece's lives in an extra slot on the same bone at that place (`*_back`, `*_under`); one whose place matches uses the base slot",
  "evidence": "where the piece and the layer are both alpha >= 250 in the set painting's See-through run: piece_shown_px = pixels where the painting's colour is nearer the piece's layer by more than 30 (sum of RGB), other_shown_px the mirror. assembly/measure.json has every layer",
  "pivot_error_px": "the bones only rotate, so the art turns about the base rig's joints; this is how far those sit from the set painting's joints at the drawn pose (shoulder: base vs set shoulder; elbow: posed sleeve_*1 origin vs set elbow). 0 at the drawn angle by construction of the attachment offsets; it grows as the bone leaves the drawn angle"
 },
 "not_expressible_in_pose6_as_written": [
  "joint positions: a set's rest pose has its own shoulder and elbow positions (pivot_error_px up to 26.6 px, K3 r elbow); pose#6 carries angles only. Translating sleeve_*0 to the set's shoulder and sleeve_*1 along its parent by the drawn upper-arm length while the set shows would make the pivots exact; rigc can key it (translate), the map has no field for it",
  "the key skeleton (`pose`) is not the drawn angle: selection by `pose` and rotation by `drawn` must be two fields"
 ],
